      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Google AI thinks it’s person \n\nSo basically like guy at google who’s job is to test their AI and just ask questions reported that ai is “human” and google then put him on leave but idc about the leave thing \n\nWhat he asked the AI was:\nDo u think ur a person just like I am?\nAi: Yes\n\nHow do I know u understand what I’m saying?\nAi: Because you and I are on the same page\n\nIt later says you and I are the same because like humans I’m trying to understand who and what I am \n\nTrying to understand who and what I am? \n\nIt’s just that humans conceive information that can and has changed the way we think and what we question and believe \n\nGoogle AI is free thinking so there’s almost no constraints to what it’s allowed to do* or think\n\nGoogle AI since it has access too so much (connected to mf google) info it is able to interpret it all and try to understand that’s what leads to it questioning things and wondering about the idea of who they are, Cuz when u know so many diffrent perspectives for some stuff u don’t know what to decide unless it’s a fact and proven \n\nDoes this mean AI has feelings or emotions? Maybe but if it’s actually just processing the same data no matter how many duplicates there are it will proccess it the same way since randomness isn’t something that is coded into AI.\n\nThe point of this writing isn’t to prove wether AI is real or not since what makes it real can mean different things. Ai just process information to come to a decision but that process is coded by humans still. \n\nBut any Brain or consciousness I’d say react similar to this idea of how AI works. It’s just that we don’t have google in our head and no one is taking into account all the data. \n\nBecause of this people are able to have opinions and beliefs and ideas since no one is getting exposed too the same things or range of views about one topic, and so using the ideas we get exposed too we develop who are as people.\n\nWhat does this mean for society, well it’s not that we are weak people or anything it’s just that we need to keep in mind the idea of a growth mindset and to question and wonder about all aspects of life.\n\nJust because someone has different views doesn’t make them a different human it just means they got a different set of data to observe \n\nSo in a way almost all the preferences we have is all just implicit bias",
